I am back in my apartment.
It is Sunday evening, and it is very quiet here.
I am standing out in the kitchen.
I wash my new plates in the sink.
These plates are really beautiful.
They are blue and a little heavy.
I dry them with a tea towel.
Afterwards, I put them in the cupboard.
I walk into the living room and look out the window.
The sun is slowly going down over the city's roofs.
This summer evening is beautiful and bright.
I really like this neighborhood.
I have lived here for half a year now.
So much has happened since January.
Back then I knew no one in the city.
Now I know the streets and everyday life much better.
I feel completely at home in this city.
Tomorrow is Monday, and I take the bus to work.
But right now I am just relaxing.
I am completely content with my life here.
